update public.questions q
set explanation = v.e
from (values
('70744a09-131c-44d6-bf4f-ec98dac646c3', 'Beyond the limit of proportionality the wire is in the plastic region. Plastic deformation is permanent, so the wire does not return to its original length.'),
('7124049c-886c-41d4-b043-78e320fa624e', 'Efficiency = useful energy out ÷ energy in = 600 J ÷ 800 J = 0.75, so 75%. The 133% option is the inverse ratio (800 ÷ 600), which cannot exceed 100% for a real device.'),
('722187e5-fd62-4eee-85cf-1b6b418ac342', 'pV = nRT with n = 1 mol, R = 8.31 J mol⁻¹ K⁻¹ and T = 300 K gives 8.31 × 300 = 2493 J. The 8.31 J option is nR alone, with T dropped.'),
('730d7551-16db-4086-b8f4-aa1ced2b3ffa', 'The normal approximation to B(n, p) uses mean np and variance np(1 − p). Here 100 × 0.5 = 50 and 100 × 0.5 × 0.5 = 25, so the mean is 50 and the variance is 25.'),
('7313c862-9894-4988-8cda-4839faf4cb5a', 'The wave equation v = fλ rearranges to λ = v ÷ f = 340 ÷ 512 ≈ 0.66 m. The 512 m option multiplies the frequency by the speed instead of dividing.'),
('731e3809-8c0d-4b54-83a1-e02baabd1e1f', 'The range is the largest value minus the smallest: 19 − 4 = 15. The 19 option is the maximum alone, which is not a measure of spread.'),
('73e1ab25-91b5-439e-ab0f-2951a9182270', 'The volume of a cuboid is length × width × height = 2 × 3 × 4 = 24 m³. The 9 m³ option adds the three sides instead of multiplying them.'),
('73f56f5b-5cbf-45b6-af4f-93527ab78ef6', 'Differentiating e^(2x) gives 2e^(2x), and differentiating again gives 2 × 2e^(2x) = 4e^(2x). Each derivative of e^(2x) brings down a factor of 2 from the chain rule.'),
('74110b4a-b178-438f-8532-37262eb14892', 'This is the absorption law: A + A·B = A(1 + B) = A, since 1 + B = 1. Any sum containing the term A·B collapses back to A.'),
('74e01fe6-bb31-42ca-90b8-3fefce7d82ab', 'Stepwise refinement is top-down design: a problem is broken into smaller sub-problems at each step. The result is hierarchical modules, not bytecode, hash tables or one monolithic block.'),
('75cf1b0b-72dd-42c8-bb6b-f312d97d86a7', 'Visible light covers roughly 400 nm (violet) to 700 nm (red). The 10–400 nm band is ultraviolet, and 700 nm–1 mm is infrared, so neither matches the visible range.'),
('75d8e72e-ade4-4903-bd50-ff196c6edc45', 'Resolving a force into two perpendicular components gives two smaller forces, F cos θ and F sin θ, whose vector sum is the original force.'),
('76d47d10-bdeb-4df6-aaf8-14f7165ecaae', 'The back bearing is the forward bearing ± 180°. Since 200° is greater than 180°, subtract: 200° − 180° = 020°. The 380° option is not a valid bearing, because bearings lie between 000° and 360°.'),
('775b047c-fb14-41d6-9172-8d2d7c7494ed', 'Ohm''s law gives R = V ÷ I = 6 V ÷ 0.5 A = 12 Ω. The 0.083 option is I ÷ V, the reciprocal of the correct ratio.'),
('77dee9cb-f44c-442a-94e6-8e52ae23edf1', 'The integral of 1/x is ln x, so the definite integral is ln e − ln 1 = 1 − 0 = 1. The answer is a single number, not an expression in e.'),
('7844e773-d87f-469e-88e9-b41348d12ab1', 'A binomial distribution needs a fixed number of trials, independent trials and a constant success probability p. A variable p breaks the model, so that is the one that is not a condition.'),
('78644f6f-bf18-426b-aaa2-4a537226974a', 'One byte is 8 bits, the standard definition used for memory sizes. Each extra bit doubles the number of distinct values a byte can store.'),
('7960a355-fdee-4797-9bb2-93c15b42231e', 'Equilibrium means the net force is zero, so there is no acceleration in any direction. The weight mg is one force within the system, not the resultant.'),
('79790927-eff3-4157-a6c3-9d517838c02b', 'For a Poisson distribution the variance equals the mean, so Var = 6 and σ = √6 ≈ 2.449. The option 6 is the variance, not the standard deviation.'),
('7ac1ba11-5da9-48ef-b483-c0cbd94ee9d7', 'Dividing gives 7 ÷ 8 = 0.875, and multiplying by 100 gives 87.5%. The 78% and 80% options are not equal to 7/8.'),
('7b79d978-ca7c-475e-aa95-716769ca451f', 'Inserting after a known node only rewires two pointers, which takes constant time, O(1). Searching for the node first would be O(n), but the question says the node is already known.'),
('7c7917f0-5d15-42a6-8083-b17c46ac3f39', 'The double-angle identity is sin 2A = 2 sin A cos A. The sin²A option is a different expression and is not equal to sin 2A.'),
('7d3eccac-37e4-4444-bf34-8ff5263b978e', 'fg(x) means apply g first, then f. g(2) = 2 + 3 = 5, and then f(5) = 5² = 25.'),
('7e504ec5-a88d-4fc9-aec0-a33729f4e0e0', 'Complement rule: P(A′) = 1 − P(A) = 1 − 0.6 = 0.4. The 0.24 option multiplies 0.6 by 0.4 instead.'),
('7f74b773-d9c5-4b35-b44a-5c3e25f75361', 'Q = mcΔT = 1 kg × 4200 J kg⁻¹ K⁻¹ × 10 K = 42 000 J. The 4200 J option is mc alone, without the temperature change.'),
('80da8489-4787-44ad-bb1a-e8b240099413', 'A probability density function must be non-negative everywhere and integrate to 1 over its range. Continuity and symmetry are not requirements for a valid density.'),
('811721fd-793b-4704-bd52-b0ef520e0a4c', 'Choose the 2 girls from 5: C(5,2) = 10. Choose the 3 boys from 6: C(6,3) = 20. The total is 10 × 20 = 200. The 462 option is C(11,5), which ignores the girl restriction.'),
('8172192d-5782-487d-8d6f-0d3842673188', 'With θ in radians the sector area is A = ½r²θ, which is the fraction θ/2π of the full circle area πr².'),
('82e4bd34-1362-44b2-96e8-038869f56745', 'Factorise: (x − 2)(x − 3) = 0 gives x = 2 or x = 3. Check: 2² − 5(2) + 6 = 0.'),
('8359eeb4-7798-49a1-b161-719b5b01b4ee', 'Expanding R sin(x + α) gives R cos α = 3 and R sin α = 4. So R² = 3² + 4² = 25 and R = 5.'),
('83cc91fa-c347-46f7-95b8-d0931d932fdf', 'A larger sample gives a smaller standard error, σ/√n, so the sampling distribution of the mean is narrower around μ.'),
('83e2a456-7bae-4fe7-94e1-316c72505002', 'The centre of gravity is the single point through which the object''s weight appears to act. It is not necessarily the geometric centre or the point of contact.'),
('8434ccf8-3f2c-47e5-8c28-d9b1ff93d589', 'Newton''s law of gravitation is F = Gm₁m₂/r². The force falls off with the square of the distance, not with the distance itself.'),
('85267493-ac0b-4492-be78-a5d9805f5d31', 'Uncompressed size = pixels × bits per pixel = 100 × 100 × 8 = 80 000 bits. The 10 000 bits option counts the pixels and ignores the 8 bits per pixel.'),
('852b41b8-14d9-4917-b177-94aa0f74ed99', 'A linear search checks items one at a time, so in the worst case it examines all n items: O(n). The O(log n) option describes binary search on sorted data.'),
('86140e63-7969-4785-a839-2dc440371a0d', 'Differentiate term by term: d/dx(5x²) = 10x and d/dx(−3x) = −3, giving 10x − 3.'),
('864c6e0e-ea87-4310-904a-b127cf82d8e0', 'The discriminant is b² − 4ac = 9 − 20 = −11, which is negative. A negative discriminant means there are no real roots.'),
('884ec867-401c-447d-a826-3ba0398c645d', 'The diffraction grating equation is d sin θ = nλ, where d is the slit spacing and n is the order of the maximum.'),
('88b72458-7ba6-4240-89fe-06b9f8f71f75', 'For a uniform distribution on [a, b] the mean is (a + b)/2 = (1 + 5)/2 = 3.'),
('88e4f70a-e8db-4dbb-a906-f27bbb41e9d1', 'Wavelength from λ = v ÷ f = 600 ÷ 200 = 3 m. The 0.33 option is f ÷ v, the inverse of the correct ratio.'),
('8a01dec8-3880-4936-bc4b-db5ac4f48dae', 'Multiply the numerators and the denominators: (2 × 3)/(3 × 4) = 6/12 = ½. The 12/6 option inverts the result.'),
('8b7fda6e-c860-478a-a9e1-b4b1ded0f408', 'Distance = √((8 − 2)² + (9 − 1)²) = √(36 + 64) = √100 = 10. The 6 and 8 options are only the horizontal and vertical differences.'),
('8bdd551d-d477-4c65-b08b-4813e378477f', 'Refractive index n = c ÷ v = (3.0 × 10⁸) ÷ (2.0 × 10⁸) = 1.5. The 0.67 option is the inverse, v ÷ c.'),
('8bfdb66d-2f1c-4d0c-a7db-538314d689e4', 'gf(x) means apply f first, then g. Substituting the expression for f(x) into g gives (2x + 3) − 1 = 2x + 2.'),
('8d9a51fa-f727-4971-9c71-4bf9245951a6', 'For parametric equations dy/dx = (dy/dt) ÷ (dx/dt) = 3t² ÷ 2t = 3t/2. Differentiating x and y with respect to t is the key step.'),
('8f190c12-2140-4d6c-b58f-ac64b19600d1', 'The grouped mean is x̄ = Σfx ÷ Σf = 420 ÷ 30 = 14. The 0.071 option is 30 ÷ 420, with the two quantities swapped.'),
('8f64c1b5-0897-40f3-83ce-b62d640fe2ad', 'Radians: 150 × π/180 = 5π/6. Since 150° = 180° − 30°, the answer is π − π/6 = 5π/6.'),
('903ba617-97f5-4629-8f01-d1c0c363cc2e', 'The standard result ∫ 1/(x + a) dx = ln|x + a| + c applies to a linear denominator. Differentiating ln|x + 2| returns 1/(x + 2) to confirm it.'),
('9069e37b-cd13-462b-98fe-3a489039d3b8', 'Stationary points occur where dy/dx = 3x² − 3 = 0, giving x = ±1. Both values are needed, so x = 0 alone is wrong.'),
('908ee465-14d7-43e3-b241-fb7250e415f7', 'Using v = u + at with u = 5 m s⁻¹, a = 2 m s⁻² and t = 4 s gives v = 5 + 8 = 13 m s⁻¹.')
) as v(id, e)
where q.id = v.id::uuid;
